// docs/spec/en/07-constexpr-and-consteval.md (ch09) §9.1(4): "A function or
// constructor declared `consteval` is an immediate function. Every
// potentially-evaluated call to it shall produce a constant expression."
// docs/spec/en/06-constant-evaluation.md (ch06) §7.2(6.2): during required
// constant evaluation "the implementation shall support ... calls to
// `consteval` functions and constructors".
//
// Call position: namespace-scope initializer. A namespace-scope `constexpr`
// initializer *requires* a constant expression ([dcl.constexpr]/6), so this
// position cannot be satisfied by a runtime evaluation at all -- the value
// must be folded during translation.
//
// Expected value derived from the spec text above and independently confirmed
// with `clang++-22 -std=c++26`, which compiles this exact source and exits 42.
consteval int twice(int x) {
    return x * 2;
}

constexpr int folded = twice(21);

int main() {
    return folded;
}
